# Files kept in the repo but not needed by the deployed site.
# The aircraft SVGs are the editable SOURCE for the sprites, which ship inlined as
# base64 data URIs inside index.html — nothing ever fetches these files at runtime.
sprites/

# Local-development only: the standalone Node CORS proxy and the Windows launcher.
# Production uses the serverless function in api/proxy.js instead.
#
# The leading slash on /proxy.js is LOAD-BEARING. .vercelignore uses .gitignore
# syntax, where a pattern containing no slash matches a file of that name at ANY
# depth — so a bare `proxy.js` also matched `api/proxy.js` and excluded the
# serverless function from the deployment. Every /api/proxy request then returned
# 404, and since the direct-to-upstream fallback was deliberately removed, that
# left the live site with no aircraft, no ISS and no geocoding at all.
/proxy.js
/START.bat
/QUICKSTART.md
/CSP-DRAFT.md
